# Testing and quality

Applies to tests and CI. Command lists live in `README.md` / `CONTRIBUTING.md`; `verify-change` chooses which ones to run.

- Test behavior a caller can observe: HTTP status and body, worker `state`/`result`, rendered loading/error/success. Do not assert on private helper structure.
- Add or update a regression test when fixing a bug. Cover the failing input.
- Mock only at external boundaries (network, Redis, Postgres, LLM). Do not mock the service under test.
- Web changes: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm format:check` in `apps/web`.
- API changes: `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run ruff format --check .`, `uv run pytest` in `apps/api`.
- Schema changes: include an Alembic revision and say whether `alembic upgrade head` ran.
- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) already runs web lint/typecheck and API Ruff/Pytest. Do not add a workflow just to document a rule.
- Report commands that ran, their result, and checks that were skipped. Never claim a green suite that was not executed.
